# Track only what is needed to reproduce the article's tables and figures:
# the R scripts, the C++ core, the input data and the READMEs.
# Results, figures, caches, manuscripts and local material stay out of Git.

# Ignore everything, then re-include the code.
*
!*/
!*.R
!*.cpp
!.gitignore
!README.md
!R/Data/*.csv

# Local folders that may hold copies of the code or generated output.
/archive/
/results/
/figures/
/manuscripts/
/submissions/
/docs/
/scripts/
/logs/
/output/
/fbst_v2/
/parallel_logs/
/build/
/outputs_articulo/
/_respaldo/
.Rproj.user/
